WEBVTT

00:00:11.991 --> 00:00:12.691
The card vault.

00:00:14.343 --> 00:00:16.050
At the checkout there is a small box:

00:00:16.519 --> 00:00:17.970
save card for faster checkout.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.359
Tick it, and your card has to live somewhere.

00:00:21.127 --> 00:00:22.492
That place is the card vault:

00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:25.266
one locked store whose only job is to

00:00:25.308 --> 00:00:26.290
hold full card numbers.

00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:31.813
For a saved card, the shop and the

00:00:31.856 --> 00:00:33.648
order system keep only a stand-in:

00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:35.696
a token, and a masked number.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.236
When the card is charged,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.411
the payment service hands the token to the

00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:40.990
vault, gets the card number back,

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:42.612
and passes it to the processor.

00:00:43.252 --> 00:00:45.001
Only the payment service talks to the vault.

00:00:48.471 --> 00:00:49.324
The vault is ours:

00:00:49.665 --> 00:00:51.500
we run it ourselves, not a processor.

00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:53.591
It holds about six hundred and eighty

00:00:53.676 --> 00:00:54.700
thousand saved cards.

00:00:55.297 --> 00:00:57.004
Only about one in seven is on an

00:00:57.047 --> 00:00:57.772
active subscription.

00:00:58.412 --> 00:01:00.161
And three in ten have already expired.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.643
It grows every year, and it has never

00:01:05.771 --> 00:01:06.471
been pruned:

00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:08.715
fifty thousand cards saved in twenty

00:01:08.843 --> 00:01:11.317
twenty-two, nearly two hundred thousand so

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.060
far this year.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.859
Yet the card security standard asks us to

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.309
keep only what the business needs.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:20.854
So a cleanup has been decided,

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:21.981
in two stages.

00:01:22.732 --> 00:01:24.865
First, the cards of members who have left,

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:26.102
and expired cards.

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:29.558
Then, valid cards unused for six months.

00:01:30.198 --> 00:01:32.460
Together, about seven in ten of the vault.

00:01:32.929 --> 00:01:34.806
Cards on an active subscription stay.

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:36.329
And nothing is deleted yet:

00:01:36.585 --> 00:01:38.207
it waits for written sign-off.

00:01:40.774 --> 00:01:41.474
The card vault:

00:01:42.012 --> 00:01:43.505
one locked place for the card number,

00:01:43.974 --> 00:01:45.766
a token for the shop, and soon,

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:47.788
only the cards we need.

